            "reason": "Confirmed, not refuted. At /home/user/bordercall/morphometry/pedicle.py:565-566, `pitch = hypot(d[0], d[1])` and `pedicle_angle_sagittal = atan2(d[2], pitch) - atan(wall_slope)`. With d = -(across, 1, rise)/n from axis_from (line 512), across = tan(t) from the walls' line and rise = b from parting, this is atan(b cos t): the axis's elevation above the transverse plane, not the angle of the climb in the sagittal plane, atan(b). Three things in the same change define the projection: the phantom truth (morphometry/tests/phantom.py:126, d = (side tan t, -1, tan s), so ped_s = atan(d_z/|d_y|)), the module docstring (\"the sagittal angle is the climb's angle to the transverse plane\", climb being dz per mm of y along the centre line, so atan(b)), and the transverse angle on line 565 (atan2(side d0, -d1), a projection). The parent commit 0e847cd^ reported the projection, `atan2(d[2], -d[1])`, with pitch = |d1|/hypot(d1,d2); the raster bias it fixed came from the fitted middles, not from that formula. The parting's b is exactly tan(s) for a tilted cylinder (translation along d shifts z by d_z/d_y per unit y at fixed x'), so the whole error is in the final formula. Computed with the code's construction (venv snippet): t 12 / s 6 reads 5.87 against 6.00 (-0.13, Shapes); t 30 / s 3 reads 2.60 (-0.40, an L5); t 27 / s 13 reads 11.62 (-1.38, a T1); t 30 / s 15 reads 13.06 (-1.94); t 45 / s 9 reads 6.39 (-2.61, a cervical pedicle). It is a wrong number, not cosmetic: a silent, one-signed under-read that grows with the transverse angle and does not average out; the morphometry/__main__.py alias maps pedicle_angle_sagittal to the papers' pedicle_incl_trans, whose Zindrick, Olsewski, Lien and Mitra rows are read on a lateral view (research_notes/paper-tables readings), i.e. the projection. Scope is honest: no current test fails on it (Straight has t = 0; Shapes loses 0.13 of its 1.5 degrees) and at the lumbar levels the 229-study run reads it is under half a degree; at cervicothoracic levels with transverse angles of 27 to 50 degrees it passes TOL_DEG. The finding's split is also right about height: for the phantom's elliptical cylinder the vertical chord is ped_h / (ez . eh) and ez . eh = hypot(d0, d1) = cos(elevation) (0.97412 at t 30 / s 15, where cos(projection) is 0.96593), so `pitch` is correct for `height` and only its comment (\"the cosine of the sagittal angle\") is wrong. Fix as proposed: report atan2(d[2], -d[1]) for the angle, keep hypot(d[0], d[1]) for the height, and say in the comment and the docstring why the two differ."
