        "problem": "climb returns 0.5 * (slopes[0] + slopes[1]) however far the top's and the bottom's slopes lie apart. The two surfaces are parted independently and, on a coarse lattice, quantise at different phases (in the synthetic probe one phase read 0.0 and the next 22.6 for the same truth), so a top of 0 and a bottom of 25 come out as a plausible 12.5 with no flag. The prototype's own log shows the pattern in the 'LP taken' column (top 0.04, bottom -1.76; 0.02 against -0.71), and only the choice of rows, not any check, keeps it out of the 'near' column. On real masks the pedicle's top and bottom over the isthmus rows are close to parallel, so their disagreement is a check outside the computation that costs nothing.",
