            "refuted": false,
            "reason": "Confirmed in the code, not refuted. /home/user/bordercall/morphometry/pedicle.py:566 now computes math.atan2(d[2], pitch) with pitch = math.hypot(d[0], d[1]) (line 561); the committed diff (0e847cd) shows the old line was math.atan2(d[2], -d[1]). axis_from (lines 486-495) builds d = -(across, 1, rise)/|d| with rise = b, the parting's dz/dy, so atan2(d[2], -d[1]) = atan(b) is the sagittal projection exactly, while atan2(d[2], hypot(d[0], d[1])) = atan(b * cos t) is the elevation. The phantom's truth is the projection: phantom.py line 126 builds the axis as (side*tan(ped_t), -1, tan(ped_s)) and truth() line 262 sets pedicle_angle_sagittal = ped_s. Running axis_from's construction in the venv: Shapes (t 12, s 6) reads 5.87 against 6.00 (0.13 low, inside TOL_DEG 1.5, so Shapes.test_pedicle_angles cannot tell the two apart); t 25/s 10 reads 0.92 low, t 30/s 10 1.32 low, t 30/s 15 13.06 (1.94 low, beyond TOL_DEG); at the transverse angles of cervical levels or S1 (t 45) 2.9 to 4.3 low. The same computation shows the transverse angle at line 565 (atan2(side*d[0], -d[1])) still returns the projection t exactly, so the two angles now follow different conventions in one measure, and the wall_slope correction subtracted at line 566 is a sagittal in-plane angle, consistent with a projection, not an elevation. It matters for the measure rather than being cosmetic: the papers the level medians are set beside (research_notes/paper-tables: Olsewski \"as on an ideal lateral film\", Zindrick halves filmed laterally, Mitra lateral roentgenograms, Lien \"in the sagittal plane\") all define the projection, and pedicle_angle_sagittal is tabulated by morphobench/figures.py (ANGLES, line 32) and aliased to the paper-tables key pedicle_incl_trans in morphometry/__main__.py line 36, so L4 and L5 carry a systematic bias of the size of the whole tolerance against both the phantom's definition and the tables, and the suite, whose only tilted phantom has ped_t 12, cannot catch it. Keep pitch = hypot(d[0], d[1]) for pedicle_h (correct for the vertical chord through the elliptic cylinder) and restore atan2(d[2], -d[1]) for the angle, or else change phantom.truth and the docstring together and add a Shapes case with ped_t of 25 or more so the test can tell the two apart."
